      "target": "u1",
      "focus": ["D", "S"],
      "change": "Broaden the condition for choosing a different candidate from the current or recent location being an 'empty container' to its being any container or surface that did not reveal the needed target, and, when the recent observation/action pairs are dominated by one location type without finding the target, prefer a different visible container or surface type before returning to the same checked set. Retain the rest of u1 unchanged: the general anti-cycle move, the applicability to both single-instance and multi-instance tasks, and the preservation of returning to a known location that still contains a needed instance.",
      "reason": "The anti-revisit and coverage direction stays goal-aligned and is motivated by the missing-target failures: `P3` cycled among `P3:20`-`P3:21`, `P3:24`-`P3:25`, `P3:37`-`P3:40` and ended at `P3:outcome` step_limit, and `P6` cycled among `P6:13`-`P6:28`, `P6:30`-`P6:38` to `P6:outcome` step_limit. The scope refinement is justified because the stalled searches also occurred at non-empty containers and surfaces that merely lacked the target, not only at empty ones: in `M5` the candidate inspected drawer 1 at `S1_R05/Q7:4`-`S1_R05/Q7:5` where `S1_R05/Q7:2` showed a knife and spatula but no butterknife, and in `M2` the candidate looped over containers and countertops without ever reaching the plausible diningtable surface (`S1_R02/Q8:1`-`S1_R02/Q8:50`). The type-diversity preference addresses the concentrated same-type cycling seen in `P3`/`P6` and in `M4` at `S1_R04/Q5:48`. These conditions remain usable under the Actor's actual access (current observation plus the last two pre-action pairs and the current admissible navigation actions), and the known-target-return preservation keeps the Parent's multi-instance collection requirement intact. The remaining repeated-cycle failures in `M2`/`M4` are non-adherence under limited memory, so the clause is widened rather than replaced.",
      "to": {
        "patch": "--- a/SKILL.md\n+++ b/SKILL.md\n@@\n-- Prefer a candidate that is not shown as already checked in the recent observations; when the current or recent location is an empty container, prefer the next unexamined instance of the same container type or a different visible container/surface type before returning to the same checked set.\n+- Prefer a candidate that is not shown as already checked in the recent observations; when the current or recent location is a container or surface that did not reveal the needed target, prefer the next unexamined instance of the same container type or, when the recent pairs are dominated by one location type without finding the target, a different visible container/surface type before returning to the same checked set.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "target": "u2",
      "focus": [],
      "change": "KEEP",
      "reason": "Direct hold-and-invoke transformation is well supported: `P1:5` cooled the held plate, `P4:5` and `P5:4` heated the held tomato, and in `M3` the candidate used `heat egg 1 with microwave 1` while holding (`S1_R03/Q9:7`) and completed at `S1_R03/Q9:9` while the parent toggled the microwave to `S1_R03/P9:50`. The container-route clause addresses an observed behavior: `P2:8`-`P2:9` moved the tomato into the microwave and closed it before the required cooling and had to reopen and retrieve it (`P2:16`). The opposite-transformation clause addresses `P5:6`, which applied `cool tomato 2 with fridge 1` after heating and then re-heated at `P5:9`. `M4` supplies the clearest direct-heat contrast (`S1_R04/Q4:5`, `S1_R04/Q4:7` versus the container toggling that reached `S1_R04/P4:50`). The preservation clause keeps the successful direct-transformation pattern, and no supplied run contradicts these clauses; they are consistent with, and generalize, the Parent's existing direct-heat guidance to cooling and to placement in thermal appliances.",
      "to": null
    }
  ],
